# Python 3.9 dev/test tooling for the ci.yml python job. Locked separately
# because a resolution for 3.9 is not the same as one for 3.13, and the wheels
# have to exist for the interpreter that installs them.
# Locked output: ci-dev-py39.txt. Refresh via scripts/update-lockfiles.sh.
#
# No pytest here, deliberately. pytest 9.x requires Python 3.10, so this row
# could only ever pin 8.4.2 -- below the fix for GHSA-6w46-j5rx-g56g, with no
# 8.x backport. Keeping a vulnerable package pinned to run tests that mostly do
# not need it is the wrong trade, so the 3.9 row runs
# bindings/python/tests/run_without_pytest.py instead: the golden-corpus and
# completeness checks, which are the ones worth running on the floor
# interpreter and which never needed a framework. The error-path tests use
# pytest.raises and run on 3.10 and up, where the whole suite runs as before.
maturin
